unmixed:
By your elimination stands to-day,
Certain, unmixed, the element of grief;
I sorrow; and I shall not mock my truth

On one point and made up:
To accept my lot unmixed;
Never to drug the cup

unmask:
And get a whole world on their forgot causing;
And, when a thought would unmask our soul’s masking,
Itself goes not unmasked to the unmasking.

unmoored:
Till all the world was sea, and I a boat
Unmoored, on what strange quest I willed to float;
Who wore a many-colored coat of dreams,

unmoved:
Threw round his path her softest light.
And yet he stood unmoved and proud,
Nor love, nor wrath, his spirit bowed;

unmothered:
Among the mountains above Pelago;
Because unmothered babes, he thought, had need
Of mother nature more than others use,

unmeaning:
Dungeons may call, and guns implore;
Unmeaning now, to me,
As laughter was an hour ago,

unmissed:
On silent wings that, ere we wist,
The fleeting years had fled unmissed;
And from our hearts this cry was wrung--
